# Comparative Optimisation of the Travelling Salesman Problem Using Iterated Local Search and Genetic Algorithms

**Module:** AI for Search and Optimisation
**Author:** Yaseen Sharaf

This notebook implements and compares **Iterated Local Search (ILS)** and a
**Genetic Algorithm (GA)** for solving the Travelling Salesman Problem (TSP)
on a 50-city dataset. Both algorithms are evaluated across increasing
problem sizes on solution quality, convergence, computational efficiency
and robustness, and the difference between them is checked with formal
statistical tests rather than judged by eye.

---

## 1. Research Question

How effectively do Iterated Local Search and Genetic Algorithms solve the
Travelling Salesman Problem as problem size increases from 10 to 50 cities,
considering solution quality, convergence, computational efficiency and
robustness?

---

